   "source": [
    "# URAE Tutorial: Holonomic D-Modules & Zeilberger Creative Telescoping\n",
    "\n",
    "This tutorial explores algorithmic summation and symbolic integration via $D$-modules:\n",
    "- **Non-Commutative Weyl Algebra $A_n$**: $[\partial_i, x_j] = \\delta_{ij}\\mathbf{I}$\n",
    "- **Leibniz Product Normal Form**: $\\partial^k x^m = \\sum_{j=0}^k \\binom{k}{j} \\frac{m!}{(m-j)!} x^{m-j} \\partial^{k-j}$\n",
    "- **Zeilberger Creative Telescoping**: $L(n, S_n) F(n, k) = (S_k - 1) G(n, k)$\n",
    "- **Almkvist-Zeilberger Algorithm**: Differential creative telescoping for hyperexponential parameter integrals"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import urae\n",
    "\n",
    "# Construct coordinate operator x and derivative operator d in A_1\n",
    "x_op = urae.weyl.WeylDOperator.coordinate(num_vars=1, var_idx=0, power=1)\n",
    "d_op = urae.weyl.WeylDOperator.derivative(num_vars=1, var_idx=0, power=1)\n",
    "\n",
    "# Compute non-commutative commutator [d, x] = d*x - x*d\n",
    "comm = d_op.multiply(&x_op).subtract(&x_op.multiply(&d_op))\n",
    "print(\"Canonical Commutator [∂, x] =\", comm)\n",
    "print(\"Is identity operator 1?\", comm.is_identity())"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 2,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Run Zeilberger's algorithm on the binomial identity sum_k binom(n, k) = 2^n\n",
    "proof = urae.weyl.ZeilbergerAlgorithm.prove_binomial_sum()\n",
    "print(\"Zeilberger Recurrence Operator L(n, Sn):\", proof.recurrence_operator)\n",
    "print(\"Certified Rational Certificate R(n, k):\", proof.certificate)\n",
    "print(\"Proof Verified Successfully?\", proof.is_valid)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Compute differential annihilating ODE for I(x) = int exp(-y^2 + 2xy) dy\n",
    "ode_cert = urae.weyl.AlmkvistZeilberger.prove_gaussian_integral()\n",
    "print(\"Annihilating Differential Operator L(x, d_x):\", ode_cert.differential_operator)\n",
    "print(\"Verified?\", ode_cert.is_valid)"
   ]
  }
